            <ArticleTitle>[Mediastinal tumor revealed by myocardial infarction].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>951-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a patient with a past history of coronary atherosclerosis treated with primary angioplasty 5 hours following an inferior myocardial infarction. Echocardiography performed during the procedure revealed a mediastinal tumour invading the tricuspid, responsible for the occlusion of the right coronary. Infarction due to tumour compression is a rare presentation of mediastinal tumour. Diagnosis relies on echocardiographic, CT or magnetic resonance imaging. The prognosis is linked to the tumour pathology.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
